<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37549" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-dulcis</span></b> , e, adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>very sweet</i>, <i>luscious</i> (perh. not ante-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mel,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					13, 4, 9, § 44</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ficus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					15, 18, 19, § 72</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					14, 6, 8, § 64</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sapor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					12, 5, 11, § 23</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. absol.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedulcĭa</span></b> ,
			ium, n., <i>over-sweet
			things</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 24, 1, 1, §
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>very pleasing</i> or
				<i>delightful</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">decus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 11, 155</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedulcis eloquii suavitas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 17, 18, § 55</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 3, 56</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedulce illud genus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					2, 5, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">malum (luxuries),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. I. Cons. Stil. 2, 132</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedulce</span></b> , <i>very sweetly</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tyrrhenae volucres (i.e. Sirenes) nautis
					praedulce minantur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 5, 3, 82</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
